      "text": "To find the value of \\(ab + ac + bc\\) for the roots \\(a, b, c\\) of the polynomial equation \\(3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas relate the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots.\n\nFor a cubic polynomial of the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\), Vieta's formulas tell us that:\n- The sum of the roots \\(a + b + c = -\\frac{b}{a}\\),\n- The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time \\(ab + bc + ca = \\frac{c}{a}\\),\n- The product of the roots \\(abc = -\\frac{d}{a}\\).\n\nIn our polynomial \\(3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0\\), the coefficients are \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = -3\\), \\(c = 11\\), and \\(d = -8\\).\n\nFirst, we use Vieta's formulas to find the sum of the roots:\n\\[\na + b + c = -\\frac{b}{a} = -\\frac{-3}{3} = 1.\n\\]\n\nNext, we use Vieta's formulas to find the sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time:\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = \\frac{c}{a} = \\frac{11}{3}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(ab + ac + bc\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{11}{3}}.\n\\]",
